The fact that Samba is tested and found working on 7.0 does not necesarrily
imply that
the binaries builds on 6.x does work.

The "normal" on VMS is that executables once build and working will continue to
work on newer VMS versions. But ther are exceptions. And an application-type
like Samba could be one of them.

It is a fact that f.ex. PathWorks server do have some VMS dependencies.

